text.section:
Where a school board undertakes a career and technical education project by contract with a corporation, the school board may advance, contribute and loan funds to the corporation. The contract shall contain:

a system of accounting;


the terms upon which any profits from the sale of the project will be allocated between the school board and the corporation;


conditions for the return with interest of any funds advanced by the school board;


a provision that upon the dissolution of the corporation, any assets remaining after payment of just debts shall be transferred to and become the property of the school board;


a provision that, upon the completion of any project, the school board may determine not to participate in further projects;


a provision that the school board may at any time require the return of funds to which it is entitled.
